    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2018-10-03T13:14:19.577Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Some months ago, before the cameras, people started creating smartphones with cameras on them to take selfies, and I have one model with that functionality too. \nnow it would be pretty nice, if the pictures taken with that could be saved to a local folder (e.g. the default camera one). \n\nThis could be achieved, by making a VRC_Trigger action... but those are not available on avatars... yet?\n\nI also see a good use case in some worlds, like the photo world, where there is a place, which shows a image as screespace shader, to make a screenshot of it. That could be made easier.\n\nI also am aware of the risks, that come with that... people could make worlds (should be controlled by VRChat team), that take a ton of images and destroy/slow down someones VRChat or whole PC. On avatars it is even more threatening, since avatars are not controlled, and people could just upload spam avatars.. :/\n...\nbut I think trashy/spam avatars will always be there and this camera would not really make it worse.",
